 **Reviewable output:** Return the question/outcome, input-manifest digest, active method/model version, selected source/graph snapshot and trust tier, cited normative expectations, relevant paths and conditional consequences, proposed investigation/test/manual/policy updates, unsupported gaps, per-claim confidence basis, safe next evidence to collect and human owner. Read analysis and native record mutation remain distinct operations. A proposed result cannot silently change Policy, Manual, Case, Skill, Model or execution state. Reuse existing permissions and shared staging/apply.
 
-**Approved is not activated; source is not assignment:** For any governed Model Studio or Skill-assisted operation, the service resolves an explicitly selected, **currently activated approved revision**, not whichever revision was approved most recently. A saved Draft, an approved but unactivated revision, an archived revision and a locally supplied method are distinct from the effective assignment. Pin the exact active revision ID, content digest, scope and decision receipt to each attempt. If an activation changes between context retrieval and a protected write, recheck server-side and require a fresh authorized selection; never silently follow "latest". A reviewer may compare proposed revisions without promoting or running them. A missing or ambiguous effective assignment must be reported as UNKNOWN/BLOCKED for the affected governed action, while authorized raw observations remain recordable.
+**Approved is not activated; source is not assignment:** Governed Skill authoring resolves the applicable **currently effective assigned approved method revision**. Model Studio **CURRENT applicability** resolves the explicitly active approved model revision. These are distinct native owners and selection rules. Preserve authorized Draft inspection/preview and explicit HISTORICAL generation/dispatch of an inactive approved model revision under MBT-C02 and the required separate consent; those paths do not activate it. A saved Draft, approved but unactivated successor, archived revision and locally supplied method never silently become the CURRENT/effective selection. Pin each attempt's actual selected revision ID, digest, mode, scope and relevant decision/consent receipt. Revalidate the relevant mode, action, authority and exact revision at the native protected-write boundary; an effective-assignment/CURRENT activation change requires fresh authorized selection or an explicit stale result, not silent substitution. Historical consent and revision validity are checked under their own retained contract rather than an unrelated active pointer. Missing/ambiguous effective method assignment blocks the affected governed authoring action; missing CURRENT selection blocks that mode while independently authorized preview/historical work and raw observations remain available under their own rules.
 
 **Separate learning evidence from generation:** Tester corrections, rejected suggestions, original case versions, before/after expected observations, reviewer rationale and genuine execution outcomes are append-only attributable learning evidence independent of regenerated candidates. Regeneration, deduplication, case replacement, Skill rollback or model switch must not erase or relabel that history. A correction may produce a proposal, but only the existing exact human review and separate activation process can change the effective guidance. A candidate's performance must be assessed against independent outcomes rather than its own regenerated examples.
 
